A||||1||FieroPerformance||Dust cover for flywheel?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||10-30-2001||05:43 PM||||When I bought my 85 GT it had an Isuzu 5 speed on it, with no dust cover for the flywheel. Is this because the dust cover does not fit properly over this transmission or would any I pull of a V6 work?<P>Second question, does anyone have one that they want to sell? How much?<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||10-30-2001||06:31 PM||||This is <B>purely</B> a guess, but I wonder if whoever did the V6 swap just forgot to put the cover on?  Another pure guess, is that the flywheel covers might be identical for both 4-cyl & 6-cyl applications?  I think  most all of the other engine-to-trans. interfaces match.  A call to your friendly GM dealer can get you the part number(s) - see if they match.<P>If I had a choice, I would start with a flywheel cover from a 4-cyl/Isuzu car, since the cover bolts to the transaxle, not the engine.  Maybe you can get one from a salvage yard, with the agreement that, if it doesn't fit, you can return the part and get your money back.  It shouldn't be an expensive part.  You have to remove the starter and 4 bolts, to get the cover out.    ||||reg||1
